Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-02
Subject: Pass tnode.getcopy's self through a local var to satisfy C++ var-binding
License: expat

`tnode.getcopy` passes `self` to `foreachnodestatic`'s `var n: tnode`
parameter. Pascal allows this; C++ does not, because `this` is `T*
const` and cannot bind to a `T*&` parameter slot.

Materialise a local `tnode` variable seeded from `self` and pass that
to the var parameter. The Pascal-side semantics match
(foreachnodestatic walks the subtree by reading `n` and the helper
function it calls writes only to local fields, never reseating `n`),
so the round-tripped slot stays consistent.

--- a/compiler/node.pas
+++ b/compiler/node.pas
@@ -908,8 +908,11 @@ implementation
 
 
     function tnode.getcopy : tnode;
+      var
+        cur : tnode;
       begin
         result:=dogetcopy;
-        foreachnodestatic(pm_postprocess,self,@cleanupcopiedto,nil);
+        cur:=self;
+        foreachnodestatic(pm_postprocess,cur,@cleanupcopiedto,nil);
       end;
 
 
